      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like the 'fairness' argument is kind of a smokescreen to stop people from improving their situation. if a kid is stuck in a failing school, why is 'protecting the system' more important than actually helping that kid get out? isn't it a bit hypocritical to call it 'fairness' when it actually keeps everyone stuck in a broken setup?",
