      "content": "That is a very strong and common critical perspective on the \"pro-system\" argument. Proponents of the status quo often argue that the *improving the system universally* is the most ethical way to ensure fairness for the entire community, not just for one family.\n\nSkeptics, like you, argue that advocating for a \"fair system\" can sometimes function to defend a system that is inherently biased or under-resourced for certain needs, effectively prioritizing the institutional structure over the immediate needs of the most struggling students.",
